Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ak7375: preserve runtime idle across system sleep

System resume calls the runtime resume implementation directly, enabling
supplies for an idle lens while runtime PM still reports it suspended.
Apollo kernel19 observed both rail use counts remain1 for20s after s2idle;
normal focus controls before sleep passed300 cycles across three boots.

Use paired runtime-PM system-sleep helpers. Already-suspended idle devices
remain idle; in-use devices suspend and restore their state through the
existing callbacks, which retain the AK7377 post-mode settling interval.
Do not change regulator routing, voltages, focus values or error handling.

Reference: https://kernel.org/doc/html/next/power/runtime_pm.html
Native validation on Apollo is required; this does not prove optical focus.

---

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ak7375.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ak7375.c
@@ -367,7 +367,7 @@
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, ak7375_of_table);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops ak7375_pm_ops = {
-	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(ak7375_vcm_suspend, ak7375_vcm_resume)
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(ak7375_vcm_suspend, ak7375_vcm_resume, NULL)
 };
 
